Transmission electron microscopy (TEM) was carried out to investigate the effect of ITCPTC content in acceptors on the morphology of blend films, as shown in Fig. 5a. No obvious aggregation can be observed for the binary and ternary blend films, indicating the good compatibility of used materials PBDB-T, IDT6CNM and ITCPTC. The fibrillar features can be clearly observed from the PBDB-T:IDT6CN-M blend films. It is very interesting that flocculent features can be clearly observed from the PBDB-T:ITCPTC blend films. The fibrillar and flocculent features can be simultaneously observed from the optimized ternary blend films, which should be mainly related to the molecular distribution of PBDB-T in the ternary blend films. Two dimensional grazing incidence X-ray diffraction (2D-GIXD) was used to study molecular
